As a regular patch writer, and also a (supposed) maintainer of
PatchHack, let me tell you that it is a whole lot easier to throw
together a patch for a cool new idea than it is to go through the
laborious process of taking a whole bunch of existing patches, making
sure they are portable and bug free, and getting them to place nice
together.

That's a lot less fun. Which is the reason why there hasn't been a new
PatchHack for ages. That and recently everytime time I start work on
it, L comes out with another slew of really popular patches which I add
to my list.

I don't suppose life is any easier for the real DevTeam. You can call
me lazy if you like, but if you're waiting for me to do all the work,
then I say: "Pot, kettle, black."

